---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Dura Fence Metal"
  description="How Dura Fence Metal uses the name, phone, email, and project details you enter on a quote request or an estimate."
>
  <article class="frame page-open">
    <p class="kicker">Dura Fence Metal</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-lg text-muted">
      <p>The quote form asks for your name, phone, email, city, and a short description of the fence or gate.</p>
      <p>The estimate page can email you the estimate PDF. That message uses the name, phone, email, and project address entered on the sheet, and a copy goes to the shop.</p>
      <p>As you type the project address, we send the address text to Photon to show suggestions. When you email an estimate, we check the full address with the U.S. Census Geocoder.</p>
      <p>That information is used to answer the request. It is not sold, and it is not added to a mailing list.</p>
      <p>If the page cannot deliver the message, nothing from the form is stored on the site. The text stays in your browser until you copy it or leave the page.</p>
      <p>We use the Meta Pixel to measure visits and the performance of our Facebook ads. Meta receives page views and an event when a quote request or estimate email is successfully sent. Our code does not include your form details in these events.</p>
      <p>Meta may use cookies and browser information to measure ads and relate website activity to its services. See <a class="link-quiet" href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/">Meta’s Privacy Policy</a> for information about its use of data and privacy controls.</p>
      <p>We use Google Analytics to measure visits, including which pages are opened. The tag does not include the details you type into a form. Google may use cookies and browser information for that measurement. See <a class="link-quiet" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10">
      <a class="link-quiet" href="/quote/">Back to the quote form</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
